# Model curves of Fig. 5, Zhao et al., PLB 789 (2019) 426 -- read from the vector PDF.
# alpha is the amplitude of the paper's Eq. (2),
#   A_LU = (dsig+ - dsig-)/(dsig+ + dsig-) = alpha sin(phi)/(1 + beta cos(phi) + gamma cos(2phi)),
# with A_LU already divided by the beam polarisation, Eq. (4).  Hence
#   alpha = sqrt(2 eps (1-eps)) * sigma_LT' / (sigma_T + eps sigma_L),  NOT the bare ratio.
# columns: model  channel  Q2  -t(GeV^2)  alpha
#   model:   0 = GK (black),  1 = GGL (red)
#   channel: 0 = eta (solid), 1 = pi0 (dashed)
# Bezier control nodes for the solid curves, polyline vertices for the dashed ones;
# interpolate, do not treat as data points.  Digitising accuracy ~0.003 in alpha.
# The GGL eta curve is absent in the two low-Q2 panels -- it is not drawn in the figure.
